{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Guides"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Derive an event’s conformances and schema from its declaration with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and constrain which values its properties may hold.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","isActive":true},{"text":", part of ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") makes a struct an event from its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declaration, and is how you declare one. It adds the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Decodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conformances, the event’s name, consent category and schema version when you give them, and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"schema","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", an ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventSchema","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value that tooling reads:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import Traffluent","","@Event(name: \"checkout_started\", version: 2)","struct CheckoutStarted {","    var cartSize: Int","    var coupon: String?","}","","let tracker = Tracker()","tracker.track(CheckoutStarted(cartSize: 3, coupon: nil))","let properties = CheckoutStarted.schema.properties.map(\\.name)  \/\/ [\"cartSize\", \"coupon\"]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The schema holds the name, the version, the consent category and each stored property’s name, its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type as written, its optionality and whether it has a default value, in declaration order. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance writes each of those properties under its name (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","type":"reference"},{"text":"). An","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"optional’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is left out, a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Date","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property, or each date in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"[Date]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"[Date?]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written as the seconds since 2001 it holds, so it reads back exactly, and a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps its redaction. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Date","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the macro doesn’t reach, inside a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type of your own or in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event whose ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance Swift synthesizes, takes the CBOR package’s own form, seconds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"since 1970, and reads back to within a rounding of a microsecond’s scale. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" protocol’s documentation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shows the conformance written by hand. A record stored before a property with a default value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"var currency: String = \"USD\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") was added reads it as its default.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version:"},{"type":"text","text":" counts breaking changes only, and is 1 when left out; "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents"},{"type":"text","text":" shows each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"kind of change. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"consent:"},{"type":"text","text":" sets the event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"consentCategory"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event(consent: .advertising)"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A stored property whose type isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a compile error that names it:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"static method 'requireCodable(position:)' requires that 'Coordinate' conform to 'Decodable'","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"So are ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on anything but a struct, and a stored property without a type annotation. Static","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and computed properties are left out. The struct keeps its memberwise initializer.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Constraining-properties","level":3,"text":"Constraining properties","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A property’s type says what kind of value it holds; a constraint says which values of that kind","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are valid. A rule the type can enforce belongs in the type: a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Refined","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value satisfies every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"constraint of its ","type":"text"},{"code":"Refinement","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from the moment it is made. Rules a plain ","type":"text"},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" can’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"carry are declared beside the property with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Constrained","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","type":"reference"},{"text":"), and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracker checks them:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["enum CouponCode: Refinement {","    static var constraints: [Constraint<String>] {","        get throws(InvalidConstraint) { try [.pattern(\"^[A-Z0-9]{6}$\", example: \"SPRING\")] }","    }","}","","@Event(name: \"search_performed\")","struct SearchPerformed {","    @Constrained(.minLength(1), .maxLength(200))","    var query: String","    @Constrained(.minimum(0))","    var resultCount: Int","    var coupon: Refined<String, CouponCode>?","}","","let coupon = try? Refined<String, CouponCode>(\"spring\")  \/\/ nil: UnsatisfiedConstraint.pattern","let tracker = Tracker()","tracker.track(SearchPerformed(query: \"\", resultCount: 3, coupon: try Refined(\"SPRING\")))","await tracker.finish()","for await report in tracker.rejectionReports {","    print(report)  \/\/ search_performed: \"query\" breaks minLength 1 (1 rejected)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The keywords are JSON Schema’s: ","type":"text"},{"code":"minLength","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxLength","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (in Unicode scalars) and ","type":"text"},{"code":"pattern","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a string, ","type":"text"},{"code":"minimum","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"maximum","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a number, ","type":"text"},{"code":"minItems","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxItems","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for an array. Each is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"offered only for the types it applies to, with its bound in the property’s own type, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".minLength","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"code":".minimum(0.5)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", is a compile error. In ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Constrained","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so is a lower bound above its upper bound, a pattern that doesn’t compile, and a pattern whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"example","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" it, or another keyword of the property, rejects. Built at run time, as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Refinement","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"‘s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are, a constraint with an argument no JSON Schema could state (a negative length, a bound that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"isn’t finite, a pattern that doesn’t compile or doesn’t match its example) throws","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"InvalidConstraint","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":"Refined","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"‘s initializer throws the ","type":"text"},{"code":"UnsatisfiedConstraint","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of the first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"constraint a value breaks, or ","type":"text"},{"code":"invalidConstraint","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when the rule’s constraints throw.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Rejected-events","level":3,"text":"Rejected events","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tracker’s worker checks each event’s declared constraints before anything else, never on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"caller. An event that breaks one is rejected: never enriched, held by a consent, written to a store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or delivered. Each rejection is reported on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracker.rejectionReports"},{"type":"text","text":" as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RejectionReport"},{"type":"text","text":" naming"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the event, the property and the keyword, and in debug builds it is logged at error level too."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Unread reports merge, one per event, property and keyword, counting the rejections and the range of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"times they were tracked, so a broken call site in a loop can’t fill memory."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record that a store recovered from an earlier run is checked again, and the store forgets one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that a constraint added since rejects. A stored "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Refined"},{"type":"text","text":" value whose rule no longer accepts it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t decode, and the store reports it. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" property takes no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Constrained"},{"type":"text","text":" keywords,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"since checking one would reveal it; a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive<Refined<…>>"},{"type":"text","text":" enforces its rule as it is made."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both kinds of constraint are part of the event’s schema. The exported tracking plan lists them"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"beside each property’s type, and each example payload satisfies them, using a pattern’s "},{"code":"example","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow"},{"type":"text","text":"). An array’s "},{"code":"Refined","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" elements are checked as they are made, but their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rules aren’t exported."}]}]}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"title":"Defining Events","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents"},"references":{"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PersistingRecords":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so a record the app tracked survives the process ending."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Persisting Records","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords"},"doc://EventMacros/documentation/EventMacros":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Derive an event’s conformances, name and schema from its struct declaration, and declare the constraints its properties satisfy."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/eventmacros","title":"EventMacros","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","role":"collection"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SamplingEvents":{"title":"Sampling Events","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","abstract":[{"text":"Keep a seeded fraction of the events a tracker tracks, event by event or a whole session at once.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/samplingevents","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SessionsAndStandardContext":{"title":"Sessions and Standard Context","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","abstract":[{"text":"Stamp every event with its session and with the app, device, system, locale and network it was tracked on.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/sessionsandstandardcontext","role":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/AutomaticTracking":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/automatictracking","abstract":[{"text":"Track screen views, control activations and the app’s lifecycle without a call at each place they happen.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Automatic Tracking","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingPlanWorkflow":{"title":"Exporting and Checking a Tracking Plan","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","abstract":[{"text":"Tell the people and services that read your events what each event holds, and hear about a change that would break their data before it ships.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow","role":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"title":"Traffluent","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","role":"collection"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ChangingEvents":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An event’s version counts the changes that records stored before them can’t be read through, and only those. A compatible change keeps the version; a breaking one raises it."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Changing an Event","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ConsentGating":{"title":"Consent Gating","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","abstract":[{"text":"Deliver an event only once the user grants the purpose it is collected for.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/consentgating","role":"article"}}}